-- title:
--   A q_N-expansion algebra map on the level-N function field
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ (an `NeZero` instance) and write $A_N :=$ [`ModularCurve.LevelN.ring N`](def/ModularCurve_LevelNFunctionField.html#L28) for the $\mathbb{C}$-subalgebra of functions $\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{C}$ generated by the modular invariant $j(\tau)=E_4(\tau)^3/\Delta(\tau)$ together with the functions `fricke N v` for all nonzero $v\in(\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ (the level-$N$ Fricke functions). Let $K$ be a field which is simultaneously a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra and an $A_N$-algebra, compatibly (a scalar tower $\mathbb{C}\to A_N\to K$), and which is a fraction field of $A_N$. The assertion is that there exists a morphism of $\mathbb{C}$-algebras $E\colon K\to\mathbb{C}((q))$ into the Laurent series field with two properties. First, $E$ sends the image in $K$ of the distinguished generator `jGen N` (namely $j=E_4^3/\Delta$, viewed as an element of $A_N$) to `qExpand ℂ N` applied to `jqModC ℂ`, that is, to the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(\mathrm{eisenstein4}^3\cdot\mathrm{dedekindEtaUnitInv})$ with integer coefficients read in $\mathbb{C}$ and with every exponent multiplied by $N$ (so $q$ replaced by $q_N^N$). Second, for every $F\colon\mathbb{H}\to\mathbb{C}$ lying in $A_N$ and every $m\in\mathbb{N}$ such that $F\cdot\Delta^m$ is bounded as $\operatorname{Im}\tau\to\infty$, the identity $E(F)\cdot\big(\text{$q_N$-expansion of }\Delta\big)^m=\big(\text{$q_N$-expansion of } F\cdot\Delta^m\big)$ holds in $\mathbb{C}((q_N))$, the power-series expansions `UpperHalfPlane.qExpansion N` being embedded into Laurent series via `HahnSeries.ofPowerSeries`.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle at the cusp $i\infty$ for the field of modular functions of level $N$: the $q_N$-expansion map $F\mapsto(\text{expansion of }F\Delta^m)/(\text{expansion of }\Delta)^m$ on $A_N$ extends to a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra map from the fraction field into $\mathbb{C}((q_N))$, normalised by the expansion of $j$. It is used downstream to compute valuations of $j$ at the place given by the cusp and to produce the Laurent-series base-change homomorphisms attached to the level-$N$ function field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_LevelN_exists_algHom_laurentSeries_qExpansion.lean

